Per-unit guest sampler state in the D3D12 backend, for all 16 fragment texture units.

The guest-FP root signature had 4 fixed static samplers (s0 point/clamp, s1-s3 linear/wrap) and a 4-wide SRV
window, so NV4097_SET_TEXTURE_FILTER / ADDRESS / CONTROL0 / BORDER_COLOR never reached a sampler and units 4-15
were not bound at all. Now: a shader-visible sampler heap holds one descriptor per distinct guest sampler state
(deduplicated, never overwritten); bind_texture computes the unit's heap index from its registers; each draw
record carries 16 indices; the replay binds s0-s15 as 16 one-descriptor root tables (root params 3..18) and the
SRV window is 16 wide (t0-t15). Draws on the built-in atlas/colour PSs keep the old defaults.
Mapped: min/mag/mip filter, anisotropy (1..16x), LOD bias (signed 4.8), min/max LOD (4.8), wrap/mirror/clamp/
border/mirror-once per axis, border colour (ARGB8). Not mapped: convolution kernels (linear), signed channels,
gamma, aniso bias, depth compare. Vertex texture units are not bound by this backend at all (separate gap).
Test: tools/smoke/host_kz3.c (four quads, units 0/9/15), KZ3 port RSX, 2026-10-07.

